 cn04) + sp80/m0r0 +1 each

Continuation of the game loop across all remaining unsolved public games,
using gpt-5.6-sol via codex (quota-limited on claude-fable-5). Operator
question: "are we making progress each round, or truly stuck." Answer for
this batch: progress, not stuck -- 4 of 10 processed so far advanced.

Full clears:
- vc33: L4 -> L7 (full clear). L5-L7 scale up the fluid-pump mechanic
  (transit-only middle pockets, a three-pocket T-junction, then a
  five-reservoir three-piece finale). Source agent honestly flagged the L7
  solve as reproduction_verified=false (budget-constrained, only 38/700
  steps left after the L1-L6 gate) -- outer loop independently ran the
  canonical gate + 4 more fresh replays, 5/5 confirmed level=7/WIN.
- cn04: L5 -> L6 (full clear). A five-sprite marker-pair puzzle solved via
  an exact-cover constraint search over marker constellations. Same honest
  unverified-but-live-observed pattern; outer loop independently confirmed
  5/5 level=6/WIN.

Level-ups (not full clears):
- sp80: L4 -> L5. The color-15 piece is a fluid elbow/diverter, not a key.
- m0r0: L4 -> L5. Small colored blocks are momentary pressure plates, not
  collectible keys (leaving a plate restores its barriers immediately).

Honest, well-investigated nulls (documented in dead_ends, not fabricated;
each genuinely narrows the search for a future attempt):
- bp35: found the missing L5 gravity switch AND its instant-death cause;
  the likely-safe click timing is untested (budget ran out after the death).
- g50t: found L4's hold-to-open tongue control, but both clone slots were
  already irreversibly committed to exploration before finding it.
- dc22: pushed further into L5 (a slab-latching bridge mechanism) but one
  dependency (a lower color-15 route) stays unresolved.
- sk48: mapped L3's two-arm block-transfer mechanism but didn't complete
  the required sort.
- sc25: TWO consecutive sessions (v18, v19) have now reached the doorstep
  of L6 and run out of energy/budget at the literal last step -- this is a
  budget-tuning problem, not a mechanically-stuck one.

Every claimed win independently re-verified per project discipline (5x
fresh env.reset() + replay via the correct GameAdapter, or the canonical
reproduction gate) before being recorded -- no self-reported agent win
trusted directly. Two more resolve_replay_plan priority branches added
(sp80, m0r0, vc33, cn04) at their new level thresholds.

reproducible_total_levels: 122 -> 128 (verified against a fresh sum).
6 of 18 round-2 games processed and committed here (bp35, cn04, dc22, g50t,
m0r0, sc25, sk48, sp80, vc33 -- 9 actually, ls20 also included); remaining
games (ka59, lf52, lp85, r11l, re86, s5i5, su15, tu93) still in flight.

